        "original_id": "2ccf0c12-d922-5c76-a046-6fc097ca3cf7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beth Robinson, Mary Bonauto, Susan Murray, Peter Shumlin\n- Products: The State of Marriage\n- Events: Baker v. Vermont, Beth Robinson's judicial nomination and confirmation\n- Organizations: Vermont Supreme Court, Vermont Senate\n- Topics: marriage equality movement, grassroots advocacy\n\nFacts:\n- Baker v. Vermont was a 1999 Vermont Supreme Court case.\n- The State of Marriage is a 2015 documentary film about the origins of the marriage equality movement.\n- The State of Marriage focuses on decades of grassroots advocacy by lawyers Mary Bonauto, Susan Murray, and Beth Robinson and on Baker v. Vermont.\n- Governor Peter Shumlin nominated Beth Robinson in October 2011.\n- The Vermont Senate confirmed Beth Robinson's nomination by a unanimous vote on February 7, 2012.",
